===== Build and install =====
Note (Dec 12, 2020): Please see the MR16 install page for an overview of the new installation process. The ath79 target will soon be supported in Snapshot and as of OpenWrt 20, and it is recommended to use it over the ar71xx target which will be deprecated after OpenWrt 19.

{{page>meta:infobox:outdated&noheader&nofooter&noeditbtn}}
{{page>meta:infobox:cleanup&noheader&nofooter&noeditbtn}}

For flashing builds after Dec 12, 2020, the following can be used to tftpboot an updated image on the MR12 for flashing.

<code>
setenv bootcmd bootm 0x9f0a0000; saveenv;
tftpboot 0x81100000 openwrt-23.05.5-ath79-generic-meraki_mr12-initramfs-kernel.bin;
bootm 0x81100000;
</code>

Once booted, you can flash the squashfs-sysupgrade.bin file from LUCI.

Note that if you previously had a mac partition for storing MAC address information in LEDE/OpenWrt, you will need to recreate the config partition with your mac at the expected offset. To do this you can use the following reference:

<code>
opkg update; opkg install kmod-mtd-rw;
insmod mtd-rw.ko i_want_a_brick=1
(
  dd if=/dev/zero bs=1 count=$((0x66)) ; # Pad the first 102 bytes
  echo -ne '\x00\x18\x0a\x12\x34\x56'  ; # Add in MAC address
  dd if=/dev/zero bs=1 count=$((0x20000-0x66-0x6)) ; # Pad the rest
) > /tmp/mac.bin
mtd write /tmp/mac.bin config;
</code>

